*! test_option_validation.cscript
*! Certification script: the value of every gated option is refused where
*! twoway refuses it, refused where a number-only option got a word twoway
*! would silently ignore, and passed through where it is a style NAME.
*!
*! ROADMAP WP-15 / GAPS.md E5.  Measured 22sep2026 (scratchpad/wp15): twoway
*! never rejects a bad style name (mcolor(notacolour), msize(abc),
*! lwidth(abc), msangle(abc) ... rc 0 plus a note), rejects out-of-range
*! numbers (msangle(400), lwidth(-1), xsize(0), bin(0), bands(201) ...) and
*! silently ACCEPTS values dash cannot use (jitter(abc|-3|101),
*! jitterseed(-1|2.5), level(0|100), lowess bwidth(5), barwidth(0), n(1)).
*! dash's declarative table (`_dash_option_rules' in dash.ado) draws the
*! line: refuse with ONE `display as error' line naming the option, exit 198
*! (111 for a variable that does not exist), never through the
*! "ignoring unsupported option(s)" note; normalise what it accepts
*! (variable abbreviations expanded, enum words lower-cased).
*!
*! Every probe registers with name(ovN): the refusal is raised before any
*! JSON is written, and the normalised value is read back out of the
*! registry global dash_json_ovN.  Each case is one line: the command, the
*! expected rc, the option the refusal must name, and (where the table
*! normalises) the JSON pair the registry must carry.  Only OV-125 renders
*! (a `dash build' after a refused replace), so Python is needed once.
*!
*! Style kinds -- a NAME is never refused, a number must sit in the range
*! where the range is twoway's own; mlabposition() and fintensity() have no
*! range (twoway accepts 13, 2.5, 150, -5 with a note or silently, and the
*! renderer notes and defaults):
*!   OV-01  msize(large)              rc 0
*!   OV-02  msize(abc)                rc 0   (a name: the renderer notes it)
*!   OV-03  mlabsize(small)           rc 0
*!   OV-04  mlabsize(abc)             rc 0
*!   OV-05  mlabgap(2)                rc 0
*!   OV-06  mlabgap(abc)              rc 0
*!   OV-07  lwidth(thick)             rc 0
*!   OV-08  lwidth(0)                 rc 0   (the corpus writes lw(0))
*!   OV-09  lwidth(-1)                rc 198 naming lwidth() and twoway's gm_linewidth line
*!   OV-10  lwidth(abc)               rc 0
*!   OV-11  mlwidth(0.5)              rc 0
*!   OV-12  mlwidth(-1)               rc 198 naming mlwidth() and twoway's gm_linewidth line
*!   OV-13  msangle(30)               rc 0
*!   OV-14  msangle(abc)              rc 0
*!   OV-15  msangle(400)              rc 198 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-16  mlabposition(12)          rc 0
*!   OV-17  mlabposition(13)          rc 0   (unbounded: the renderer notes it)
*!   OV-18  mlabposition(2.5)         rc 0
*!   OV-19  fintensity(50)            rc 0
*!   OV-20  fintensity(inten50)       rc 0   (a name)
*!   OV-21  fintensity(150)           rc 0   (drawn darker, as twoway draws it)
*! Numeric kinds -- a word is refused, a number must sit in the range:
*!   OV-22  jitter(5)                 rc 0
*!   OV-23  jitter(abc)               rc 0 (drawn as none, WP-35 basic:PT-13)
*!   OV-24  jitter(-3)                rc 0 (drawn as none, WP-35 basic:PT-13)
*!   OV-25  jitter(101)               rc 0 (drawn, WP-35 basic:PT-13)
*!   OV-26  jitterseed(20260920)      rc 0
*!   OV-27  jitterseed(-1)            rc 0 (WP-35 basic:PT-13)
*!   OV-28  jitterseed(2.5)           rc 0 (WP-35 basic:PT-13)
*!   OV-29  jseed(7)                  rc 198 naming jseed() (DT-15)
*!   OV-30  jseed(abc)                rc 198 naming jseed()
*!   OV-31  yaxis(2)                  rc 0
*!   OV-32  yaxis(3)                  rc 0 (WP-31 C10c: axes 3-9 drawn)
*!   OV-33  xaxis(1)                  rc 0
*!   OV-34  xaxis(3)                  rc 0 (WP-31 C10c: axes 3-9 drawn)
*!   OV-35  malpha(60)                rc 198 naming malpha() (DT-15)
*!   OV-36  malpha(150)               rc 198 naming malpha()
*!   OV-37  lalpha(50)                rc 198 naming lalpha() (DT-15)
*!   OV-38  lalpha(abc)               rc 198 naming lalpha()
*!   OV-39  falpha(40)                rc 198 naming falpha() (DT-15)
*!   OV-40  falpha(-1)                rc 198 naming falpha()
*!   OV-41  base(5)                   rc 0
*!   OV-42  base(abc)                 rc 4026 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-43  barwidth(20)              rc 0
*!   OV-44  barwidth(0)               rc 0 (drawn, WP-35 basic:PT-13)
*!   OV-45  barwidth(abc)             rc 198 naming barwidth()
*! level() -- the rule moved from _dash_parse_plot_opts into the table:
*!   OV-46  level(90)                 rc 0
*!   OV-47  level(abc)                rc 198 naming level()
*!   OV-48  level(100)                rc 0   (as twoway: no band; WP-31 C10a)
*!   OV-49  level(0)                  rc 0   (as twoway; WP-31 C10a)
