*!   OV-63  kdensity kernel(gaussian) rc 0
*!   OV-64  kdensity kernel(Epan2)    rc 198, "use kernel(epan2)" (DT-15)
*!   OV-65  kdensity kernel(bogus)    rc 198 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-158..162 kernel(gau) registered in full, kernel(EPAN) refused (DT-15);
*!          gaussianx, gau;rm and a 253-letter word refused (WP-27), in
*!          twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-66  kdensity n(50)            rc 0
*!   OV-67  kdensity n(1)             rc 0   (as twoway; WP-31 C10a)
*!   OV-68  kdensity n(abc)           rc 198 naming n()
*!   OV-69  kdensity n(20000)         rc 198 naming n()      (dash's own limit)
*!   OV-70  histogram bin(12)         rc 0
*!   OV-71  histogram bin(0)          rc 125 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-72  histogram bin(2.5)        rc 126 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-73  histogram bin(abc)        rc 121 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-74  histogram bin(5000)       rc 198 naming bin()    (dash's own limit)
*!   OV-75  histogram width(3)        rc 0
*!   OV-76  histogram width(0)        rc 125 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-77  histogram width(abc)      rc 121 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-78  histogram start(10)       rc 0
*!   OV-79  histogram start(abc)      rc 121 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-80  mband bands(6)            rc 0
*!   OV-81  mband bands(0)            rc 198 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-82  mband bands(2.5)          rc 198 naming bands()
*!   OV-83  mband bands(abc)          rc 198 naming bands()
*!   OV-84  mband bands(201)          rc 198 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-85  function range(0 10)      rc 0
*!   OV-86  function range(10)        rc 122 naming range()  (twoway's; WP-31 C10a)
*!   OV-87  function range(0 5 10)    rc 123 naming range()  (twoway's; WP-31 C10a)
*!   OV-88  function range(abc)       rc 111 variable abc not found (twoway's)
*! Colour mapping and variables:
*!   OV-89  colornlevels(6)           rc 198 naming colornlevels() (DT-15)
*!   OV-90  colornlevels(1)           rc 198 naming colornlevels()
*!   OV-91  colornlevels(abc)         rc 198 naming colornlevels()
*!   OV-92  colpalette(magma)         rc 198 naming colpalette() (DT-15)
*!   OV-93  colpalette(Viridis)       rc 198 naming colpalette() (DT-15)
*!   OV-94  colpalette(bogus)         rc 198 naming colpalette()
*!   OV-95  colorcuts(20 30)          rc 0
*!   OV-96  colorcuts(abc)            rc and words of R_cuts_abc
*!   OV-97  colorvar(for)             rc 0, registry carries "colorvar":"foreign"
*!   OV-98  colorvar(nosuch)          rc and words of R_var_nosuch
*!   OV-99  colorvar(rep78 foreign)   rc and words of R_var_two
*!   OV-100 mlabel(mak)               rc 0, registry carries "mlabel":"make"
*!   OV-101 mlabel(nosuchvar)         rc 111, twoway's variable line
*! Graph rules:
*!   OV-102 xsize(9)                  rc 0
*!   OV-103 xsize(abc)                rc 0   (a name)
*!   OV-104 xsize(0)                  rc 198 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-105 ysize(3)                  rc 0
*!   OV-106 ysize(101)                rc 198 in twoway's words (WP-45 GW-1)
*!   OV-107 aspectratio(0.75)         rc 0
*!   OV-108 aspectratio(-1)           rc 198 naming aspectratio()
*!   OV-109 aspectratio(abc)          rc 198 naming aspectratio()
*!   OV-110 hover(pri wei)            rc 0, registry carries "hover":"price weight"
*!   OV-111 hover(nosuchvar)          rc 111 naming hover()
*!   OV-112 by(for, total)            rc 0, registry carries "by":"foreign, total"
*!   OV-113 by(nosuchvar)             rc 111, twoway's variable line
*!   OV-114 by(, total)               rc 100 in twoway's words (Flipped,
*!                                    WP-41 BY-6: it was r(198))
*!   Q4105-1 aspectratio() with by(, shrink|overallshrink) rc 198 in
*!                                    twoway's words (WP-41 BY-5)
*!   Q4105-2 by(, total)              rc 100 "varlist required in by()"
*!                                    (WP-41 BY-6)
*! KPI fmt() (AC-15.2):
*!   OV-115 fmt(bogus)                rc 198 naming fmt()
*!   OV-116 fmt("HACKED" %9.2f)       rc 198 naming fmt()
*!   OV-117 fmt(%9.2f)                rc 0
*!   OV-118 fmt(%12s)                 rc 198 naming fmt()
*!   OV-119 fmt(%tdCCYY-NN-DD)        rc 0
*!   OV-120 fmt(%9.0fc)               rc 0
*!   OV-163..165 fmt(%21x %16H %16L)  rc 198 naming fmt() (WP-28 S04)
*!   OV-166..168 fmt(%9,2fc %tm %10.0g) rc 0
*! The adversarial review's findings (DESIGN.md section 7.1, 22sep2026):
*!   OV-121 colorvar(L.price) jitter(5), data tsset
*!                                    rc 101, twoway's "factor-variable and
*!                                    time-series operators not allowed"
*!                                    (Flipped, WP-31 A6: it was r(198)
*!                                    naming colorvar(); A1: the old tsunab
*!                                    fallback cleared s() and registered
*!                                    the segment with no options)
*!   OV-122 colorvar(price) jitter(5) rc 0, registry carries "jitter":"5"
*!                                    AND "colorvar":"price" (the control)
*!   OV-123 colorvar(L.price) jitter(5), data NOT tsset
*!                                    rc 101 likewise (Flipped, WP-31 A6:
*!                                    it was r(111) naming colorvar())
*!   OV-124 mlabel(L.mpg) jitter(5), data tsset
*!                                    rc 111, twoway's "variable L not
*!                                    found" (Flipped, WP-31 A6: r(198))
*!   OV-125 a graph and a KPI k registered, then
*!          kpi name(k, replace) fmt(bogus)   rc 198 naming fmt(), the old
*!          KPI's globals dash_kpi_k and dash_kpi_k__fmt intact, the registry
*!          still listing k once; kpi name(k, replace) update(bogus) rc 198
*!          likewise; then `dash build, saving() replace' rc 0 and the file
*!          exists (A2: the replace used to drop the old KPI BEFORE the
*!          checks, and the next build died on a corrupt registry)
*!   OV-126 (scatter mpg weight, xsize(500)) , xsize(5)
*!                                    rc 198 in twoway's words (A3: a graph
*!                                    option inside a segment is validated
*!                                    even when a later value outranks it)
*!   OV-127 (scatter mpg weight, by(nosuch)) , by(foreign)
*!                                    rc 111, twoway's variable line
*!   OV-128 colorcuts(1(1)5)          rc 0, registry carries
*!                                    "colorcuts":"1 2 3 4 5" (A4)
*!   OV-129 kdensity range(0,10)      rc 0, registry carries "range":"0 10"
*!   OV-130 yaxis(2.0)                rc 0, registry carries "yaxis":"2" (A5)
*!   OV-131 kdensity n(1E3)           rc 0, registry carries "n":"1000"
*!   OV-132 msize(1e400)              rc 0, read as msize(0) as twoway draws
*!                                    it (WP-35 basic:PT-13, D60)
*!   OV-133 jitter(<tab>5<tab>)       rc 0, registry carries "jitter":"5"
*!                                    (A8: tabs are trimmed; twoway rc 0)
*!   OV-134 by("foreign")             rc 111, twoway's line, and the message
*!                                    reads `variable "foreign" not found'
*!                                    with nothing garbled (the old form
*!                                    quoted the name in single quotes and
*!                                    a trailing " ended the compound quote)
*! S1 -- the WP-16 adversarial review (DESIGN.md section 6.3), measured
*! 22sep2026 (scratchpad/wp16/F3/measure_twoway.log): `twoway bar price',
*! `twoway scatter mpg' and every other two-variable type say "too few
*! variables specified" r(102); histogram and kdensity take one variable.
*! dash used to register such a segment with rc 0 and die at build with a
*! Python KeyError on the empty x column, r(7102).  The refusal names the
*! PLOT TYPE, not an option, so these cases go through _ov_refused:
*!   OV-135 bar price                 rc 102, twoway's one error line,
*!                                    "too few variables specified" (the
*!                                    words were dash's own, "bar requires
*!                                    a y and an x variable (got: price)",
*!                                    until the S3 batch), nothing
*!                                    registered
*!   OV-136 bar price mpg             rc 0 (the control)
*!   OV-137 scatter mpg               rc 102 likewise
*!   OV-138 (scatter mpg weight) (bar price)
*!                                    rc 102: one short segment refuses
*!                                    the whole command
*!   OV-139 line price if foreign     rc 102: an if-clause is not a
*!                                    variable
*!   OV-140 histogram mpg             rc 0 (the one-variable types are
*!   OV-141 kdensity mpg              rc 0  untouched)
*! The scheme kind (WP-17): a shipped scheme or theme name passes as
*! written, anything else is refused before Python (the file-in-the-
*! working-directory cases are test_custom_scheme.cscript's):
*!   OV-142 scheme(s2color)           rc 0
*!   OV-143 scheme(Economist)         rc 0, registry carries
*!                                    "scheme":"Economist" (nothing normalised)
*!   OV-144 scheme(nosuchthing)       rc 0, twoway's note, s2color (ST-16)
*!   OV-145 scheme(../x)              rc 0, twoway's note, s2color (ST-16)
*!   OV-146 scheme(s2color.scheme)    rc 0, registry carries
*!                                    "scheme":"s2color.scheme" (a shipped
*!                                    name written with the extension; no
*!                                    such file in the working directory)
*!   OV-147 scheme(S2COLOR.SCHEME)    rc 0   (likewise, in any case)
*!   OV-148 scheme(nosuch.scheme)     rc 198 naming scheme() (the
*!                                    extension does not make a name: a
*!                                    name that is not shipped still needs
*!                                    the file)
*! WP-22 TR-22.3 -- the connecting-line width and the marker-label angle:
*!   OV-149 line clwidth(thick)       rc 0, registry carries "clwidth":"thick"
*!   OV-150 line clwidth(-1)          rc 198 naming clwidth() and twoway's gm_linewidth line
*!   OV-151 line clwidth(abc)         rc 0   (a name)
*!   OV-152 bar clwidth(-1)           rc 0, and no clwidth in the registry
*!                                    (bar draws no connecting line, so
*!                                    twoway never evaluates it: rc 0)
*!   OV-153 mlabangle(45)             rc 0, registry carries "mlabangle":"45"
*!   OV-154 mlabangle(400)            rc 198 in twoway's words (WP-35 basic:PT-9)
*!   OV-155 mlabangle(abc)            rc 0   (a name: twoway notes it)
*!   OV-156 line mlabangle(400)       rc 0   (twoway draws no marker
*!                                    labels on line, so never evaluates it)
*! Size forms (WP-30 S08, P1.12a): every Stata size spelling registers
*! untouched -- rc 0, no "must be" line, the spec carrying the value as
*! written (dash.ado is unchanged; the renderer reads the units):
*!   SU-01  msize(4pt)                rc 0, registry carries "msize":"4pt"
*!   SU-02  msize(*2)                 rc 0, registry carries "msize":"*2"
*!   SU-03  msize(vhuge)              rc 0, registry carries "msize":"vhuge"
*!   SU-04  msize(.1in)               rc 0, registry carries "msize":".1in"
*!   SU-05  msize(1d3)                rc 0, registry carries "msize":"1d3"
*!   SU-06  msize(HUGE)               rc 0, registry carries "msize":"HUGE"
*!   SU-07  mlabsize(*1.5)            rc 0, registry carries "mlabsize":"*1.5"
*!   SU-08  mlabgap(2pt)              rc 0, registry carries "mlabgap":"2pt"
*! Line widths (WP-30 S13, P1.12b): the forms twoway refuses, r(198) with
*! "gm_linewidth must be between 0.000 and  1.0e+04" (measured 03oct2026),
*! then dash's line naming the option; the rest register (rc 0):
*!   LN-01  lwidth(*-1)               rc 198 naming lwidth(), both lines
*!   LN-02  lwidth(-1pt)              rc 198 naming lwidth()
*!   LN-03  lwidth(-0.5in)            rc 198 naming lwidth()
*!   LN-04  lwidth(1e5rs)             rc 198 naming lwidth()
*!   LN-05  scatter mlwidth(*-1)      rc 198 naming mlwidth()
*!   LN-06  line clwidth(-1pt)        rc 198 naming clwidth()
*!   LN-07  lfitci alwidth(*-1)       rc 198 naming alwidth()
*!   LN-08  line alwidth(*-1)         rc 0   (not on alwidth()'s type list)
*!   LN-09  lwidth(10000rs|*0|0pt|-0) rc 0
*!   LN-10  lwidth(20000pt)           rc 0   (the renderer notes it, D-13b);
*!          lwidth(*40000) rc 198 as twoway (WP-35 basic:PT-13)
*!   LN-11  lwidth(vvvthin|none|THICK|1PT|-1PT|*1e400)  rc 0 (names)
*!   LN-12  lwidth(-1)                rc 198, twoway's line before dash's
*!   LN-13  scatter lwidth(*-1)       rc 0 (no line drawn; WP-35 basic:PT-13)
*!   LN-14  msize(-1pt|*-1), mlabgap(-2pt)  rc 0 (the ,u reading is the
*!                                    line options' alone)
*! The words the absence checks search for, each found where it must be
*! (24sep2026):
*!   OV-09m                           OV-09's refusal says "must be", which
*!                                    no accepted case may print
*!   OV-157 dlpattern(dash) on dot    rc 0, and OV-157m: the log says
*!                                    "unsupported option", which no
*!                                    refusal may print ("not found" is
*!                                    found at OV-134m)
*! A comma-written plot colour (WP-30 P1.13a), refused in twoway's words:
*!   CG-01  mcolor("255,0,128")        rc 198, invalid '0', nothing registered
*!   CG-02  lcolor("1,2,3") on line    rc 198, invalid '2'
*!   CG-03  mcolor("red,blue")         rc 198, invalid 'blue'
*!   CG-04  mcolor("1,")               rc 198, invalid 'editcopy'
*!   CG-05  mcolor(red "255,0,0")      rc 198, invalid '0' (two y)
*!   CG-06  mcolor("1,,2")             rc 0, registered (the renderer notes it)
*!   CG-07  bgcolor("1,2,3")           rc 0 (twoway accepts it)
*!   CG-08  mcolor(navy*.5)            rc 0, the spec carries "mcolor":"navy*.5"
*!   CG-09  fourteen blank-and-comma colour forms on five plot options and
*!          thirteen structured sub-options, each against twoway live: the
*!          rc and the refusal line twoway gives (18oct2026: twoway refuses
*!          a colour whose second, fourth ... comma-separated part is not
*!          blank, in each stylelist element a y uses, and draws the rest)
*! The corpus arbiter:
*!   CV-nn  every line of test/fixtures/conformance_corpus.txt registers
*!          with rc 0 and no refusal -- the table accepts every value the
*!          documented corpus writes -- and CV-count: every line was probed,
*!          as many as the fixture holds.
*! Option applicability (WP-31 C3), each dash line against twoway's own in
*! the same run (test/fixtures/applicability_truth.json holds every pair):
*!   U04-01  twelve pairs twoway refuses (kernel n level bwidth range base
*!           bin width start on scatter, bands on kdensity, degree on
*!           lowess, barwidth on rspike): rc 198 and the same first line,
*!           option <opt>() not allowed
*!   U04-02  twelve pairs twoway accepts: rc 0, nothing names the option
*!   U04-03  the parenthesised and || forms refuse as twoway does
*!   U04-04  the type is refused before the value: scatter kernel(nosuch)
*!           says option kernel() not allowed; lpoly kernel(nosuch) still
*!           gets the kernel's own message
*!   U12-08  gap() area() boundary droplines() baroffset() refused on a type
*!           twoway's parser does not declare them for, taken where it does
*!           (WP-31 C5; test/fixtures/kde_hist_fn_truth.json applies)
*! Value bounds (WP-31 C10a), each dash rc and line against twoway's own in
*! the same run (test/fixtures/value_bounds_truth.json):
*!   U05-04  level(): lpolyci level(5), (9.99), (100) refused in twoway's
*!           line, (10) and (99.99) taken; lfitci, qfitci and fpfitci take
*!           level(5), (100), (150), (0) and (-1), as twoway does
*!   U05-05  range(): lfit range(nosuch), (make), (weight), (10), (1 2 3);
*!           function and kdensity range(10), (1 2 3), (. 3), (nosuch);
*!           function range(make): twoway's rc and line
*!   U05-06  lowess bwidth(-1), (0), (1), (1.5), (5): rc 0 as twoway, no
*!           note naming bwidth()
*! Parsed values (WP-31 C10b; test/fixtures/parsed_values_truth.json):
*!   U06-04  yaxis(1 1), (2 1), (1 2), xaxis(1 2) taken as twoway takes them;
*!           yaxis(0), (10), (1.5), (abc) refused with twoway's rc and line;
*!           yaxis(1 2 3) drawn, as twoway draws it (flipped, WP-31 C10c)
*! Weight expressions (WP-31 A5; test/fixtures/weight_operator_truth.json):
*!   U07-7  lfit [aw=price+1] rc 0, no note; [aw=nosuch+1], [aw=price+]
*!          and kdensity [aw=nosuch*2] refused with twoway's rc and line
*!   U07-8  weight texts holding a backtick, $, ;, a double quote or a tab
*!          refused typed (Stata's weight syntax, twoway's rc), by
*!          _dash_wexp_ok, and from an edited registry at export, r(198);
*!          no __dash column left, the data kept
*!   U07-9  mlabel(L.make) on histogram, function, mspline and mband:
*!          twoway's code (WP-31 A6 guard)
*! Axes three to nine (WP-31 C10c; test/fixtures/axes_n_truth.json):
*!   U09-4  yaxis(0), (10), (2.5) and xaxis(10): twoway's rc and line; no
*!          "two axes" sentence; yaxis(9) drawn
*!   U09-5  ylabel(1 2, axis(3)) with no layer on axis 3: twoway's rc and
*!          line; with a layer on axis 3: rc 0
*!   U09-7  yaxis(3) on scatter, line, bar, rarea and histogram: rc 0 as
*!          twoway
*!   U09-8  yaxis(1 2) still taken as twoway takes it (WP-31 C10b guard)
*! The fit options (WP-31 C4; test/fixtures/fit_options_truth.json):
*!   U11-07 nofit and atobs on scatter, estopts() on lpolyci, atobs on
*!          fpfit, estcmd() on lfit: twoway's rc and line; atobs on
*!          fpfitci and smoothplot() on lpolyci taken
*! Minor ticks (WP-31 D1; test/fixtures/minor_tick_truth.json m_refusal):
*!   U24-5  xlabel(##5): twoway's rc 0 and its note "##5 ignored, only
*!          allowed for minor ticks", printed by dash when it draws
*! Edge titles (WP-31 D2; test/fixtures/edge_title_truth.json refuse_*):
*!   U27-6  title2("x") and a bare title2: twoway's rc and line
*!   U27-7  subtitle2("x"): twoway's rc and line
*!   U27-8  title2() inside a plot's parentheses and after a || segment's
*!          comma: twoway's rc and line
*!   U27-9  title("A") title("B"): rc 0 in both, and dash keeps the last
*!          copy, B, as twoway draws it (merged_title)
*! Textbox placement (WP-31 D3; test/fixtures/textbox_truth.json):
*!   U30-7  title("T", position(0) span): rc 0 in both and twoway's note
*!          "option span ignored for position(0)", printed by dash when it
*!          draws (span_pos0)
*!   U30-8  note("N", tstyle(nosuch)): rc 0 in both and twoway's note
*!          "named style nosuch not found in class textboxstyle, default
*!          attributes used", printed by dash when it draws (tstyle_bad)
*! Edge-title placement (WP-31 D2b; textbox_truth.json e_t1_span):
*!   U30-14 span and nospan inside an edge title: twoway's rc and line,
*!          "option(s) t1title_span(yes) not allowed"

*! Legend geometry (WP-31 D4; test/fixtures/legend_geometry_truth.json):
*!   U31-10 legend(symxsize(bogus)): rc 0 in both; twoway notes "named
*!          style bogus not found in class gsize" and dash, drawing, names
*!          legend(symxsize(bogus)) as not a recognised size
*!   U31-11 legend(holes(0)) and holes(2.5): twoway's rc and words,
*!          "holes() invalid -- invalid numlist has ..."
*! Sizing (WP-31 D5; test/fixtures/sizing_truth.json):
*!   U32-6  scale(-1) refused in twoway's gm_linewidth line, fxsize(x) and
*!          fysize(x) in "option fxsize() incorrectly specified"; scale(0),
*!          scale(x), fxsize(150) and fysize(0) drawn, as twoway draws them
*!   U32-7  aspectratio(1, foo) refused "option foo not allowed";
*!          aspectratio(1, placement(xx)) drawn with twoway's note
*!   U32-11 (WP-31 C8d) pcycle() with a fraction on 1, 2, 3, 4 and 16
*!          series, and a ci fit counted as two: dash's rc is twoway's
*!          (pcycle_fraction_truth.json)
*! Graph-wide refusals (WP-35 section 35-06; graph_refusal_truth.json),
*! each command on the one-line route and with name():
*!   Q3506-1 (basic:PT-8) two omit options anywhere in one command refused
*!          r(198) in twoway's words; one drawn as twoway draws it
*!   Q3506-3 (GW-3) maxaxes() checked as twoway checks it: no integer
*!          r(198), an axis above it r(125); a valid one drawn, not named
*!   Q3506-5 (sil:SD-8) a title, subtitle, note or caption with notitling
*!          refused r(4018) in twoway's words; notitling alone named
*!   Q3506-7 (syn:SD-22, documented) contour and contourline refuse an
*!          option they do not know with levels() too, which twoway ignores
*! Statistical-type refusals (WP-35 section 35-04; stat_refusal_truth.json):
*!   Q3504-1 (stat:PT-1) histogram's bins() with width(), and two of
*!          density, fraction, frequency and percent, refused r(198) in
*!          twoway's words
*!   Q3504-2 (stat:PT-2) density, fraction, frequency and percent refused
*!          off histogram, r(198), "option <word> not allowed"
*!   Q3504-5 (stat:PT-14) bw() refused off lowess, lpoly, lpolyci and
*!          kdensity, r(198), "option bw() not allowed", and on bar, rbar,
*!          histogram, dot and spike a second line "use barwidth()"
*! Value refusals in twoway's codes (WP-35 section 35-05;
*! value_codes_truth.json):
*!   Q3505-1 (basic:PT-9) every probe twoway refuses there, dash's rc and
*!          first line twoway's: mlabel(make..), rbar barwidth(.), lfit
*!          and kdensity and mspline n(), and lwidth(-1), mlwidth(-1) and
*!          msangle(400) on each type twoway refuses them on
*! The spellings twoway refuses that dash took (WP-35 section 35-07;
*! dash_only_words_truth.json):
*!   Q3507-1 (DT-15) ytitle2() .. ttitle2(), marker(), malpha(), lalpha(),
*!          falpha(), jseed(), mlg(), cv(), colv(), colornlevels(),
*!          colormissing(), plotbgcolor(), pbgc(), colpalette(),
*!          kernel(GAUSSIAN), xsize(()) and a string colorvar() refused
*!          with twoway's rc and line and a line naming twoway's spelling,
*!          inside p1() too, in twoway's order
*! The colorvar() values twoway refuses (WP-42 section 42-05, CV-9;
*! colorvar_refusal_truth.json, every rc and line read from it):
*!   Q4205-2a..2j  colorcuts(abc), colorlevels(abc), colorlevels(2.5),
*!          colorvar(rep78 foreign), colorvar(pri*), colorvar(price-length),
*!          colorvar(nosuch), colorvar(pri) (drawn), colorvar(make),
*!          colorvar(L.price): twoway's rc and lines, nothing more
*! The colorvar spellings and layers (CV-14; DECISIONS.md P4-7, P4-9):
*!   Q4205-4a..4e cv(), colv(), colornlevels(), colormissing(),
*!          colpalette(): twoway's line and the hint line (HINT)
*!   Q4205-4f a string colorvar(): twoway's rc and line
*!   Q4205-4g a colorvar() layer with no observation (E_*): twoway's rc
*!          and lines, then the line naming the plot
*!   Q4205-4h colordiscrete and all-missing layers are drawn
*! mlabel() on the immediate types (WP-47 MS-7):
*!   Q4701-4  scatteri, pci, pcarrowi mlabel(nosuch) rc 0; mlabel(..),
*!          mlabel(=) twoway's r(198) and line
*! twoway's older spellings (WP-47 basic:PT-10):
*!   Q4704-4  a bad value of symbol(), msymangle(), bcolor(), afcolor(),
*!          bfintensity(), afintensity(), blwidth(), blpattern(), bmsize()
*!          rc 0, unnamed; mlabels(nosuchvar) r(111), twoway's line
*! Refusal first lines (WP-49 plot:PT-7, test/fixtures/refusal_line_truth.json):
*!   Q4901-1  an option spelled short at each refusal site: twoway's rc
*!          and first line, the option as typed (option ba() not allowed)
*!   Q4901-2  value_truth.json's TR-10 rows: no line after the first
*!   Q4901-3  the syn:SD-12 first lines are twoway's; the dropped dash
*!          sentences print no second line
*!   Q4901-4  the Supported list still follows "is not a twoway plot type"
*!   Q4901-5  the kept second lines (unknown, repeated, refused synonym)
*!
*! Every refusal is read back out of a captured log with Stata's wrapped
*! lines re-joined, as test_suboption_reporting.cscript does.
*!
*! Usage:  via run_all_cscripts.do (the dash directory must be on the
*!         ado-path).

cscript "dash option validation" adodir ".."

clear all
// Certification timing: run_all_cscripts.do reads timer 100 when this
// script ends; with DASH_CERT_PROFILE set it also prints the profile.
timer clear 100
timer on 100
local _cert_prof : environment DASH_CERT_PROFILE
if "`_cert_prof'" != "" {
    capture profiler clear
    profiler on
}
set more off


do "cert_helpers.do"
qui do "../dash_parse.mata"
qui do "../dash.ado"

global dash_nobrowser 1
sysuse auto, clear

// The conformance corpus draws range plots, paired coordinates and a time
// series against these; test_conformance.cscript builds the same set.
quietly generate double lo = mpg - 3
quietly generate double hi = mpg + 3
quietly generate double w2 = weight + 250
quietly generate double m2 = mpg + 4
quietly generate int    t  = _n
quietly tsset t

// The tally lives in two globals rather than the do-file's locals: with
// one line per case a helper program does the counting, and a program
// cannot read its caller's locals.  Both are dropped in the summary.
// (A global's name cannot start with an underscore -- measured, r(198) --
// so these two carry the script prefix without it.)
global ov_nfail    = 0
global ov_faillist ""

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Log scanner: re-join "> " continuations, then count the logical lines
// that carry `needle' and hand back the first.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
capture mata: mata drop _ov_scan()
capture mata: mata drop _ov_json_has()
capture mata: mata drop _ov_tlc()
mata:
void _ov_scan(string scalar fn, string scalar needle)
{
    real scalar   fh, n
    string scalar line, full, first
    fh = fopen(fn, "r")
    n = 0
    full = ""
    first = ""
    while ((line = fget(fh)) != J(0, 0, "")) {
        if (substr(line, 1, 2) == "> ") {
            full = full + substr(line, 3, .)
            continue
        }
        if (strpos(full, needle)) {
            n = n + 1
            if (first == "") first = full
        }
        full = line
    }
    if (strpos(full, needle)) {
        n = n + 1
        if (first == "") first = full
    }
    fclose(fh)
    st_local("_ov_n", strofreal(n))
    st_local("_ov_line", first)
}

// Does the registered spec for graph `g' carry the text `needle'?
real scalar _ov_json_has(string scalar g, string scalar needle)
{
    return(strpos(st_global("dash_json_" + g), needle) > 0)
}

// Does the command text carry a comma outside every parenthesis?  A
// segment's own comma (inside its parentheses) does not count: name() is
// then still the first graph-level option and needs the comma written.
real scalar _ov_tlc(string scalar s)
{
    real scalar   i, depth
    string scalar c
    depth = 0
    for (i = 1; i <= strlen(s); i++) {
        c = substr(s, i, 1)
        if (c == "(") depth = depth + 1
        else if (c == ")") depth = depth - 1
        else if (c == "," & depth == 0) return(1)
    }
    return(0)
}
end

capture program drop _ov_count
program define _ov_count, rclass
    version 16.0
    args logfile needle
    mata: _ov_scan(st_local("logfile"), st_local("needle"))
    return scalar n = `_ov_n'
    return local line `"`macval(_ov_line)'"'
end

capture program drop _ov_has
program define _ov_has, rclass
    version 16.0
    args g needle
    mata: st_local("_oh", strofreal(_ov_json_has(st_local("g"), st_local("needle"))))
    return scalar found = `_oh'
end

// Run one command with the log captured and judge it:
//   rc must equal `expected';
//   a refusal (expected != 0) must name `opt'() and must NOT be the
//   ignoring note;
//   an acceptance (expected == 0) must print no refusal at all.
// Every probe starts from an empty registry.
capture program drop _ov_probe
program define _ov_probe, rclass
    version 16.0
    args id cmdtext expected opt
    local logfile "`c(tmpdir)'dash_ov.log"
    set linesize 80
    capture log close _ovlog
    capture erase "`logfile'"
    capture dash clear
    log using "`logfile'", name(_ovlog) text replace
    capture noisily `cmdtext'
    local rc = _rc
    log close _ovlog
    local bad = 0
    if `rc' != `expected' {
        display as error `"`id' FAIL: expected rc `expected', got rc `rc': `macval(cmdtext)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    if `expected' != 0 {
        // With the blank before it: every refusal reads "dash: <opt>() ..."
        // (fmt()'s, "dash kpi: fmt() ..."), and without it "width()" was
        // found in "barwidth()" and "n()" in "bin()", so a refusal naming
        // the wrong option passed.
        _ov_count "`logfile'" " `opt'()"
        if r(n) == 0 {
            display as error `"`id' FAIL: the refusal does not name `opt'()"'
            local bad = 1
        }
        _ov_count "`logfile'" "unsupported option"
        if r(n) > 0 {
            display as error `"`id' FAIL: a refused value was reported as an unsupported option: `r(line)'"'
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
    else {
        _ov_count "`logfile'" "must be"
        if r(n) > 0 {
            display as error `"`id' FAIL: an accepted value was refused: `r(line)'"'
            local bad = 1
        }
        _ov_count "`logfile'" "not found"
        if r(n) > 0 {
            display as error `"`id' FAIL: an accepted value was refused: `r(line)'"'
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
    return scalar bad = `bad'
    return scalar rc  = `rc'
end

// One case: probe, then (when a needle is given) assert the registry
// carries the normalised pair -- two needles where two pairs must survive
// together.  Tallies into the two globals.
capture program drop _ov_case
program define _ov_case
    version 16.0
    args id cmdtext expected opt needle needle2
    _ov_probe "`id'" `"`macval(cmdtext)'"' `expected' "`opt'"
    local bad = r(bad)
    local rc  = r(rc)
    local nm = "ov" + subinstr("`id'", "OV-", "", 1)
    foreach nd in needle needle2 {
        if `"`macval(`nd')'"' != "" & `bad' == 0 {
            _ov_has "`nm'" `"`macval(`nd')'"'
            if r(found) != 1 {
                display as error `"`id' FAIL: the registered spec does not carry `macval(`nd')':"'
                mata: st_global("dash_json_" + st_local("nm"))
                local bad = 1
            }
        }
    }
    if `bad' {
        global ov_nfail    = ${ov_nfail} + 1
        global ov_faillist "${ov_faillist} `id'"
    }
    else {
        display as text `"`id' PASS: rc `rc' -- `macval(cmdtext)'"'
    }
end

// The log of the case just probed must carry `needle' (the wording of a
// refusal, beyond the option it names).  Its own id, so a case that fails
// on both counts is tallied twice, once per assertion.
capture program drop _ov_said
program define _ov_said
    version 16.0
    args id needle
    _ov_count "`c(tmpdir)'dash_ov.log" `"`macval(needle)'"'
    if r(n) == 0 {
        display as error `"`id' FAIL: the log does not say `macval(needle)'"'
        global ov_nfail    = ${ov_nfail} + 1
        global ov_faillist "${ov_faillist} `id'"
    }
    else display as text `"`id' PASS: the log says `macval(needle)'"'
end

// One hand-rolled assertion outside _ov_case (OV-125 keeps a registry
// across several commands, which _ov_probe would clear).
// _u46_rc id expected cmdtext (WP-31 C11): the command's return code
// alone, into the log _ov_said reads -- a refusal in twoway's words names
// no option the way dash's "dash: <opt>() ..." does.
capture program drop _u46_rc
program define _u46_rc
    version 16.0
    args id expected cmdtext
    local logfile "`c(tmpdir)'dash_ov.log"
    capture log close _ovlog
    capture erase "`logfile'"
    capture dash clear
    log using "`logfile'", name(_ovlog) text replace
    capture noisily `cmdtext'
    local rc = _rc
    log close _ovlog
    _ov_assert `id' "(`rc' == `expected')" `"rc `rc' (expected `expected') -- `macval(cmdtext)'"'
end

capture program drop _ov_assert
program define _ov_assert
    version 16.0
    args id cond what
    if `cond' {
        display as text `"`id' PASS: `macval(what)'"'
    }
    else {
        display as error `"`id' FAIL: `macval(what)'"'
        global ov_nfail    = ${ov_nfail} + 1
        global ov_faillist "${ov_faillist} `id'"
    }
end

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// WP-42 section 42-05 (CV-9, CV-14): a colorvar() value, spelling or
// layer run through dash as test/fixtures/colorvar_refusal_truth.json ran
// it in twoway.  _q4205 <id> <key> [<hint> [<plot line>]]: dash's rc is
// twoway's, and on a refusal dash prints twoway's lines, then the hint
// line test/dash_only_rulings.py's HINT holds for <hint> (P4-9), then
// <plot line> (37-01's line naming the plot), and nothing else.  Every
// expectation is read from the fixture or HINT, never typed.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
python:
import json as _q4205_json
from sfi import Macro as _q4205_M
from dash_only_rulings import HINT as _q4205_hint
with open("fixtures/colorvar_refusal_truth.json", encoding="utf-8") as _q4205_fh:
    _q4205_fx = _q4205_json.load(_q4205_fh)["probes"]


def _q4205_take(key):
    c = _q4205_fx[key]["command"].strip()[len("twoway "):].rstrip()
    if c.endswith(","):
        c = c[:-1].rstrip()
    _q4205_M.setLocal("q_cmd", c)
    _q4205_M.setLocal("q_rc", str(_q4205_fx[key]["rc"]))


def _q4205_judge(key, path, rc, hint, plot):
    r = _q4205_fx[key]
    lines = []
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as fh:
            for ln in fh:
                if ln.strip() and not ln.startswith((". ", "> ")):
                    lines.append(ln.strip())
    except OSError:
        pass
    want = [ln.strip() for ln in r["lines"]]
    if hint:
        want.append(_q4205_hint[hint])
    if plot:
        want.append(plot)
    ok = int(rc) == r["rc"] and (r["rc"] == 0 or lines == want)
    _q4205_M.setLocal("q_ok", "1" if ok else "0")
    for name, text in (("q_got", " / ".join(lines)),
                       ("q_want", " / ".join(want))):
        for ch, to in (('"', "'"), ("\x60", "'"), ("$", "S")):
            text = text.replace(ch, to)
        _q4205_M.setLocal(name, text[:300])
end
capture program drop _q4205
program define _q4205
    version 16.0
    args id key hint plot
    python: import __main__ as _q4205_main; _q4205_main._q4205_take("`key'")
    // The cases around it keep their data.
    preserve
    quietly sysuse auto, clear
    quietly gen m = .
    quietly gen ymiss = .
    quietly gen t = _n
    quietly tsset t
    if "`key'" == "E_nodata" | "`key'" == "E_nodata_disc" quietly drop if 1
    set linesize 255
    capture dash clear
    capture log close _ovlog
    capture erase "`c(tmpdir)'dash_ov.log"
    quietly log using "`c(tmpdir)'dash_ov.log", name(_ovlog) text replace
    capture noisily dash `macval(q_cmd)'
    local rc = _rc
    quietly log close _ovlog
    python: import __main__ as _q4205_main; _q4205_main._q4205_judge("`key'", r"`c(tmpdir)'dash_ov.log", "`rc'", "`hint'", "`plot'")
    _ov_assert `id' "(`q_ok' == 1)" `"`key': rc `rc' (twoway `q_rc'); dash said: `macval(q_got)'; want: `macval(q_want)'"'
    capture dash clear
    set linesize 80
    restore
end

// A command refused at registration for its VARLIST rather than an
// option: rc must equal `expected'; the captured log must say `needle'
// (the message names the plot type and the variables given); it must
// not be the ignoring note; and nothing may be registered under the
// case's name -- the refusal comes before any JSON is written.
capture program drop _ov_refused
program define _ov_refused
    version 16.0
    args id cmdtext expected needle
    local logfile "`c(tmpdir)'dash_ov.log"
    local nm = "ov" + subinstr("`id'", "OV-", "", 1)
    set linesize 80
    capture log close _ovlog
    capture erase "`logfile'"
    capture dash clear
    log using "`logfile'", name(_ovlog) text replace
    capture noisily `cmdtext'
    local rc = _rc
    log close _ovlog
    local bad = 0
    if `rc' != `expected' {
        display as error `"`id' FAIL: expected rc `expected', got rc `rc': `macval(cmdtext)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    _ov_count "`logfile'" `"`macval(needle)'"'
    if r(n) == 0 {
        display as error `"`id' FAIL: the log does not say `macval(needle)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    _ov_count "`logfile'" "unsupported option"
    if r(n) > 0 {
        display as error `"`id' FAIL: the refusal was reported as an unsupported option: `r(line)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    if `"${dash_json_`nm'}"' != "" {
        display as error `"`id' FAIL: the refused command still registered `nm'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    if `bad' {
        global ov_nfail    = ${ov_nfail} + 1
        global ov_faillist "${ov_faillist} `id'"
    }
    else display as text `"`id' PASS: rc `rc' -- `macval(cmdtext)'"'
end

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// OV-01 .. OV-21: style kinds
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
_ov_case OV-01 `"dash scatter mpg weight, msize(large) name(ov1)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-02 `"dash scatter mpg weight, msize(abc) name(ov2)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-03 `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabsize(small) name(ov3)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-04 `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabsize(abc) name(ov4)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-05 `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabgap(2) name(ov5)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-06 `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabgap(abc) name(ov6)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-07 `"dash line mpg weight, sort lwidth(thick) name(ov7)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-08 `"dash line mpg weight, sort lwidth(0) name(ov8)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-09 `"dash line mpg weight, sort lwidth(-1) name(ov9)"' 198 lwidth
// The words every accepted case is searched for and must not print: a
// refusal says "must be" -- found here, in one that must.
_ov_said OV-09m "must be"
_ov_case OV-10 `"dash line mpg weight, sort lwidth(abc) name(ov10)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-11 `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlwidth(0.5) name(ov11)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-12 `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlwidth(-1) name(ov12)"' 198 mlwidth
_ov_case OV-13 `"dash scatter mpg weight, msangle(30) name(ov13)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-14 `"dash scatter mpg weight, msangle(abc) name(ov14)"' 0 ""
// Flipped (WP-35 basic:PT-9): r(198) in dash's words was wrong;
// twoway refuses it r(198) "symbolangle must be between -360.000 and 360.000".
_u46_rc OV-15 198 `"dash scatter mpg weight, msangle(400) name(ov15)"'
_ov_said OV-15 "symbolangle must be between -360.000 and 360.000"
_ov_case OV-16 `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabposition(12) name(ov16)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-17 `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabposition(13) name(ov17)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-18 `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabposition(2.5) name(ov18)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-19 `"dash area mpg weight, sort fintensity(50) name(ov19)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-20 `"dash area mpg weight, sort fintensity(inten50) name(ov20)"' 0 ""
_ov_case OV-21 `"dash area mpg weight, sort fintensity(150) name(ov21)"' 0 ""

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// OV-22 .. OV-45: numeric kinds
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
_ov_case OV-22 `"dash scatter mpg weight, jitter(5) name(ov22)"' 0 ""
// Flipped (WP-35 basic:PT-13): r(198) was wrong; twoway draws it as no jitter
// (value_codes_truth.json jitter_abc_ref).
_ov_case OV-23 `"dash scatter mpg weight, jitter(abc) name(ov23)"' 0
// Flipped (WP-35 basic:PT-13): r(198) was wrong; twoway draws it as no jitter
